==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|seinn}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*sainaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*sainijaz}}, related to {{m|gem-pro|*sīþuz|t=late}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/seitn/}}
* {{rhymes|is|eitn|s=1}}

===Adjective===
{{is-adj|@@}}

# [[late]], [[tardy]]
#: {{syn|is|síðkvæmur}}
#: {{ux|is|Hann hlýtur að vera kominn — hann er aldrei '''seinn'''.|t=He must be here already—he's never '''late'''.}}
#: {{ux|is|Við erum orðnar '''seinar''' í tíma!|t=We're '''late''' for class!}}
# [[slow]]
#: {{syn|is|hægur}}

====Declension====
{{is-adecl|comp}}

====Derived terms====
{{col-auto|is
|orðinn seinn
|seinn að<t:slow at>
|seinn á fæti<t:to be a slow walker>
|seinn fyrir<t:late, behind-hand>
|seinn til<t:to develop late>
|svifaseinn
|um seinan<t:too late>
}}

====See also====
* {{l|is|seinlæti}}

